# Scenario: a mortgage adviser sets the two loan types side by side before the rate conversation with a first-time buyer.
tchart "Fixed-rate or adjustable-rate mortgage"
column "Fixed-rate"
- Payment stays the same for the whole term
- Starts at a higher interest rate than an adjustable loan
- Easy to budget over 15 or 30 years
- Refinancing is the only way to benefit when rates fall
column "Adjustable-rate"
- Low introductory rate for the first 5, 7 or 10 years
- Payment resets with the market index once the introductory period ends
- Rate caps limit how far each reset can move
- Suits buyers who expect to sell or refinance early
